Subject: [PATCH 3/3] memcg: drop a duplicate mem_cgroup_allow_attach()

Enabling CONFIG_MEMCG does not compile:

    mm/memcontrol.c:6988:12: error: redefinition of 'mem_cgroup_allow_attach'
    mm/memcontrol.c:6799:12: note: previous definition was here

mem_cgroup_allow_attach() is defined three times. Twice legitimately, once in
each arm of the CONFIG_MMU conditional around the move-charge code: the MMU arm
delegates to subsys_cgroup_allow_attach(), the !MMU arm returns 0. The third sits
after the #endif, unconditionally, and is an older standalone implementation that
predates the generic helper -- it was left behind when that refactor landed.

Nobody noticed because every ASUS configuration for this board has MEMCG off, so
this file was never built.

Keeping the conditional pair and dropping the straggler is both the structurally
correct choice and the behaviourally intended one. The two implementations are
near-identical, but the generic helper admits CAP_SYS_NICE while the straggler
demanded CAP_SYS_ADMIN -- and CAP_SYS_NICE is what system_server holds when it
moves tasks between cgroups, so the helper is the one Android expects. Every
other controller already goes through it.

Also silences the "defined but not used" warning on the MMU-arm definition, which
the straggler had been shadowing at the point of use.
---
diff --git mm/memcontrol.c mm/memcontrol.c
index a19c7213..460218dc 100644
--- mm/memcontrol.c
+++ mm/memcontrol.c
@@ -6985,23 +6985,6 @@ static void mem_cgroup_move_task(struct cgroup *cont,
 }
 #endif
 
-static int mem_cgroup_allow_attach(struct cgroup *cgrp,
-				 struct cgroup_taskset *tset)
-{
-	const struct cred *cred = current_cred(), *tcred;
-	struct task_struct *task;
-
-	cgroup_taskset_for_each(task, cgrp, tset) {
-		tcred = __task_cred(task);
-
-		if ((current != task) && !capable(CAP_SYS_ADMIN) &&
-		    cred->euid != tcred->uid && cred->euid != tcred->suid)
-			return -EACCES;
-	}
-
-	return 0;
-}
-
 /*
  * Cgroup retains root cgroups across [un]mount cycles making it necessary
  * to verify sane_behavior flag on each mount attempt.
